# Short (72 chars or less) summary in imperative mood
#
# More detailed explanatory text, if necessary. Wrap to 72 characters.
# The blank line separating the summary from the body is critical.
#
# Write in the imperative: "Fix bug" not "Fixed bug" or "Fixes bug."
# This matches git merge and git revert.
#
# Further paragraphs come after blank lines.
#
# - Bullet points are okay, too
# - Use a hyphen or asterisk for bullets, followed by a single space
# - Use hanging indent for wrapped bullet text
#
# If applied, this commit will <your subject line here>
#
# Why is this change needed?
# How does it address the issue?
# What effects does this change have?
# Are there any limitations or side effects?
#
# References:
# Fixes #123
# Related to #456
# See: https://example.com/docs